Context Goals

   This document describes the context goals available in the Apache Tomcat Maven Plugin.
   These goals allow you to manage web applications deployed to a running Tomcat server.

   For running web applications with an embedded Tomcat server, see the
   {{{./run-goals.html}Run Goals}} documentation.

* {Deploying a WAR project}

  To deploy a WAR to Tomcat you can type:

+--
mvn package tomcat:deploy
+--

  This will package your project and deploy it to Tomcat. The plugin will automatically
  detect the WAR file and deploy it to the configured Tomcat server.

* {Redeploying a WAR project}

  To redeploy an existing WAR to Tomcat you can type:

+--
mvn package tomcat:redeploy
+--

  This will redeploy the WAR to Tomcat, replacing the existing deployment.

* {Undeploying a WAR project}

  To undeploy a WAR from Tomcat you can type:

+--
mvn tomcat:undeploy
+--

* {Starting a WAR project}

  To start a WAR in Tomcat you can type:

+--
mvn tomcat:start
+--

* {Stopping a WAR project}

  To stop a WAR in Tomcat you can type:

+--
mvn tomcat:stop
+--

* {Reloading a WAR project}

  To reload a WAR in Tomcat you can type:

+--
mvn tomcat:reload
+--

* {Listing session statistics}

  To list the session statistics for a deployed WAR project you can type:

+--
mvn tomcat:sessions
+--

  This will display information about active sessions for the deployed application.